From: Paulo Duarte <paulofernandobd@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 01:43:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Re-add GNU Hurd kernel support to lib/systems.

Restores the support that lived in nixpkgs from ~2012 through 2018 and was
removed in PR #45721 (commit history under pkgs/os-specific/gnu/).  This
patch is purely additive (no existing behaviour changes) and just makes
nixpkgs willing to PARSE `i686-gnu` / `x86_64-gnu` / `*-pc-gnu` /
`*-unknown-gnu` triplets and produce canonical `<cpu>-gnu` configs from
them.  The actual glibc-hurd, hurd-headers, and hurd userland packages
live in this flake under flakes/{cross-toolchain,hurd-headers,hurd}/.

Triplet choice: `i686-gnu` / `x86_64-gnu` is the canonical user-facing
form across the entire gnumach/MIG/Hurd ecosystem - upstream gnumach
building.html, upstream MIG building.html, cross-hurd's CROSS_HURD_TARGET,
Debian's DEB_HOST_GNU_TYPE for hurd-i386/hurd-amd64, Sergey Bugaev's
upstream glibc submissions, and Guix's %hurd-systems all use the 2-tuple
`<cpu>-gnu` form.  `<cpu>-pc-gnu` is what config.sub canonicalises that to
internally for autotools; `<cpu>-unknown-gnu` is a pre-canonicalisation
artefact of config.guess never used as an input.

Changes:
  - lib/systems/parse.nix: add the `hurd` kernel (ELF, no family,
    `.name = "gnu"`).  Add `gnu` as an alias (mirrors `darwin =
    kernels.macos`) so the 2-tuple `i686-gnu` resolves via the "2"-case
    catch-all.  Add a dedicated Hurd branch at the TOP of the "3"-case so
    `<cpu>-pc-gnu` / `<cpu>-unknown-gnu` parse to `kernel = "gnu"`; it MUST
    precede the cpu-kernel-environment branch, whose `elem (elemAt l 2)
    [... "gnu" ...]` (the gnu ABI) would otherwise capture Hurd's `gnu` as
    the abi with kernel=<vendor> and fail with "Unknown kernel: pc".
    Special-case `tripleFromSystem` to emit the canonical 2-tuple
    `<cpu>-gnu` for Hurd targets - drives cc.targetPrefix -> `i686-gnu-gcc`.
  - lib/systems/inspect.nix: add `isHurd` predicate; include it in `isUnix`.
  - lib/systems/default.nix: `isHurd -> libc = "glibc"` in the libc
    cascade; `|| isHurd` in `hasSharedLibraries`; uname.system entry
    `gnu = "GNU"` (keyed by parsed.kernel.name, which is "gnu").

Rebased onto nixpkgs nixos-26.05, whose parse.nix split the old single
cpu-kernel-environment allow-list into two branches and moved the `gnu`
ABI into the first one - so the Hurd 3-tuple branch now leads the "3"
case (the old "add gnu/hurd to the list" hunk is obsolete).  Expect a
one-line fuzz on next minor bumps.
---
 lib/systems/parse.nix   |   46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 lib/systems/inspect.nix |    4 ++++
 lib/systems/default.nix |    6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 54 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/lib/systems/parse.nix	2026-05-31 20:23:50
+++ b/lib/systems/parse.nix	2026-05-31 20:24:23
@@ -635,6 +635,19 @@
         execFormat = pe;
         families = { };
       };
+      # GNU Hurd.  `.name = "gnu"` matches the upstream canonical naming
+      # used by gnumach/MIG building docs, cross-hurd's CROSS_HURD_TARGET,
+      # Debian's DEB_HOST_GNU_TYPE for hurd-i386 / hurd-amd64, Sergey
+      # Bugaev's glibc upstream submissions, and Guix's %hurd-systems.
+      # The kernel attribute is still named `hurd` (so `kernels.hurd` and
+      # the `isHurd` predicate read naturally) but `.name` - which feeds
+      # tripleFromSystem -> config -> cc.targetPrefix - is "gnu" so
+      # cross-binaries land as `i686-gnu-gcc` (not `i686-hurd-gcc`).
+      hurd = {
+        execFormat = elf;
+        families = { };
+        name = "gnu";
+      };
     }
     // {
       # aliases
@@ -643,6 +656,10 @@
       watchos = kernels.ios;
       tvos = kernels.ios;
       win32 = kernels.windows;
+      # `gnu` resolves to the Hurd kernel - used by 2-tuple parsing of
+      # `i686-gnu`, the form upstream gnumach/MIG/Hurd documentation
+      # uses on its configure invocations.
+      gnu = kernels.hurd;
     };
 
   ################################################################################
@@ -826,8 +843,22 @@
             kernel = elemAt l 1;
           };
       "3" =
-        # cpu-kernel-environment
+        # GNU Hurd: `<cpu>-<vendor>-gnu` (i686-pc-gnu / i686-unknown-gnu).
+        # Must be checked BEFORE the cpu-kernel-environment branch below -
+        # that branch's `elem (elemAt l 2) [... "gnu" ...]` (the gnu ABI)
+        # would otherwise mis-match Hurd's `gnu` as the abi field with
+        # kernel=<vendor>, which then fails with "Unknown kernel: pc".
         if
+          elemAt l 2 == "gnu"
+          && (elemAt l 1 == "pc" || elemAt l 1 == "unknown")
+        then
+          {
+            cpu = head l;
+            vendor = elemAt l 1;
+            kernel = "gnu";
+          }
+        # cpu-kernel-environment
+        else if
           elemAt l 1 == "linux"
           || elem (elemAt l 2) [
             "eabi"
@@ -974,7 +1005,18 @@
       optAbi = optionalString (abi != abis.unknown) "-${abi.name}";
       cpuName = if kernel.families ? darwin then darwinArch cpu else cpu.name;
     in
-    "${cpuName}-${vendor.name}-${kernelName kernel}${optExecFormat}${optAbi}";
+    # GNU Hurd uses the 2-tuple form `i686-gnu` / `x86_64-gnu` everywhere
+    # in the upstream ecosystem (gnumach docs, MIG docs, cross-hurd,
+    # Debian's DEB_HOST_GNU_TYPE for hurd-i386/hurd-amd64, Sergey
+    # Bugaev's upstream submissions, Guix manifests).  config.sub
+    # canonicalises `i686-gnu` -> `i686-pc-gnu` internally for autotools,
+    # but the user-facing prefix (driving cc.targetPrefix) stays as the
+    # 2-tuple - so cross-binaries are named `i686-gnu-gcc`, matching
+    # what every other Hurd consumer expects.
+    if kernel == kernels.hurd then
+      "${cpuName}-${kernel.name}"
+    else
+      "${cpuName}-${vendor.name}-${kernelName kernel}${optExecFormat}${optAbi}";
 
   # This is a function from parsed platforms (like stdenv.hostPlatform.parsed)
   # to parsed platforms.
--- a/lib/systems/inspect.nix	2026-05-31 20:23:50
+++ b/lib/systems/inspect.nix	2026-05-31 20:24:23
@@ -318,6 +318,7 @@
       isSunOS
       isCygwin
       isRedox
+      isHurd
     ];
 
     isMacOS = {
@@ -371,6 +372,9 @@
     };
     isNone = {
       kernel = kernels.none;
+    };
+    isHurd = {
+      kernel = kernels.hurd;
     };
 
     isAndroid = [
--- a/lib/systems/default.nix	2026-05-31 20:23:50
+++ b/lib/systems/default.nix	2026-05-31 20:24:23
@@ -185,6 +185,8 @@
             null
           else if final.isNone then
             "newlib"
+          else if final.isHurd then
+            "glibc"
           # TODO(@Ericson2314) think more about other operating systems
           else
             "native/impure";
@@ -243,6 +245,9 @@
               wasi = "Wasi";
               redox = "Redox";
               genode = "Genode";
+              # GNU Hurd: parsed.kernel.name is "gnu" (see kernels.hurd
+              # in parse.nix); uname -s on real Hurd reports "GNU".
+              gnu = "GNU";
             }
             .${final.parsed.kernel.name} or null;
 
@@ -274,6 +279,7 @@
           (
             isAndroid
             || isGnu
+            || isHurd
             || isMusl # Linux (allows multiple libcs)
             || isDarwin
             || isSunOS
